{
  "description": "Cross-language contract for the content screen (ADR-0077): the office's content terms and number detectors, found and masked. Python: aiq_agent.common.content_screen (tests/aiq_agent/common/test_content_screen.py). TypeScript: frontends/ui/src/lib/upload-screening/content-screen.ts (content-screen.spec.ts). For each case both assert the same matches (rule and matched text, in rule order then position: terms in list order, then iban, at_svnr, credit_card), the same masked text and the same findings, and that masking the masked text changes nothing. `matches` is a single pass over `text`; `masked` and `findings` are the result of masking to a fixpoint. Matched text, not offsets, is compared because Python counts code points and JavaScript UTF-16 units. `placeholders` is defined in Python (PLACEHOLDERS) and held here so the TS mirror cannot drift. There is ONE copy: the TS spec reads this file from disk at run time (vitest runs in frontends/ui with the whole repository checked out) rather than importing it, so the frontend typecheck never needs a path outside frontends/ui.",
